* ''The ward key rides the admission'' (operator, 2026-11-06, approving the house's defaults). Each device's per-face ward public key rides its signed admission (`wardKey`, covered by `vesselSig`, the tag key's signature over group, atom and ward key) beside its proof of possession (`wardPop`), and a ward-act approval carries that key's signature over the answer, the ask's digest and the frontier the answerer read; the vessel key never enters a face admission (the fleets-overlap ruling, 2026-11-05). An approval binds one ask's digest, and the frozen spend refuses its replay. A ward key never rotates silently: a rewrap keeps the key, and a device whose ward goes missing re-joins as a new vessel (`ward-key-would-rotate`). The law rests in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seat-harness#/the-swarm-slices`>>.

